From 3650cef9acfe77eb2d34c8e491e9da6bb643c682 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Blue Cuenca <blue.cuenca@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 16:27:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 65/69] pwm: sunxi-enhance: propagate DT node to pwm_chip
 device
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

pwmchip_alloc() creates a virtual chip device whose of_node is NULL.
ops like sunxi_pwm_enable_single() call of_parse_phandle(chip->dev.of_node,
"sunxi-pwms", ...) — which returned NULL, causing -ENODEV on every
PWM enable attempt.

Copy the platform device's of_node to the chip device after allocation
so the DT lookups work correctly.

Signed-off-by: Blue Cuenca <blue.cuenca@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pwm/pwm-sunxi-enhance.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pwm/pwm-sunxi-enhance.c b/drivers/pwm/pwm-sunxi-enhance.c
index 45b0a4233..30e3d41a4 100644
--- a/drivers/pwm/pwm-sunxi-enhance.c
+++ b/drivers/pwm/pwm-sunxi-enhance.c
@@ -1002,6 +1002,9 @@ static int sunxi_pwm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
         return PTR_ERR(chip);
     pwm = pwmchip_get_drvdata(chip);
 
+    /* Propagate DT node so ops can call of_parse_phandle("sunxi-pwms") */
+    chip->dev.of_node = pdev->dev.of_node;
+
     /* io map pwm base */
     pwm->base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
     if (IS_ERR(pwm->base))
-- 
